# core/data/talk/grammar/en/warm_praise.tlk - more replies to compliments, praise of a third
# party and thanks (owner: TK; T5b package T5B-WARM). Same rules as core_warm.tlk: PG-21 adults,
# nothing a kid may not hear, no register word, at most one exclamation mark a line (the
# exclamation budget of a quiet resident), no filler that needs a guard the rule lacks.
# Syntax: core/tools/talkc_gen.py. Writing register: docs/design/story/SCRIPT_STYLE.md.

# ---- COMPLIMENT: thank -----------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.compliment.w_thank act: thank
  "Thank you. I'll wear that all day, like a hat."
  "That's kind. I'm blushing in at least three places."
  "Oh, I needed that. My morale was at two bars."
  "You're too nice. Keep going, though."
  "Thanks. I'll tell my mirror you said so."
  "Stop it. {.}Okay, don't stop it."
  "Well, that made my whole afternoon. And it's morning."
  "Thank you, truly. I'm saving that one for a bad day."
  "That means a lot. A normal amount, plus tax."
  "You really think so? Okay! Thank you."
  "Gosh, thanks. I forgot how to take a compliment. Is it a handshake?"
  "I'll treasure that. Somewhere dry, with the good spoons."
  "How sweet. My happy meter just went up a notch."
  "Thanks, I try. Mostly I trip and it works out."
  "You've made me feel like a full health bar."
  "That's lovely to hear. Say it again, slower, so I can record it."
  "Aw. You're the reason the day has a good part."
  "Thanks! I'm going to float home now. Don't wait up."
  "Oh, hush. {.}No, don't hush. Tell the others."
  "I accept this compliment and will use it wisely."
@rule core.compliment.w_thank_polite guard: polite act: thank
  "How very generous of you. Thank you kindly."
  "You're too gracious. Thank you, truly."
  "Oh, that is lovely of you to say. Thank you."
  "I'm much obliged. You've warmed up the whole room."
  "What a charming thing to say. I'm flattered."
@rule core.compliment.w_thank_flat guard: flat act: thank
  "Thanks. {.}Internally I'm doing a little dance."
  "Noted, and appreciated. Very much. This is my excited voice."
  "Huh, nice. That landed somewhere. I'm not sure where."
  "That's good to hear. I'll feel it later."
  "I'm smiling. You can't see it. Trust me."
@rule core.compliment.w_thank_loud guard: loud act: thank
  "WOW! Thank you! Say it to the whole park."
  "You're the BEST! I mean, I am. But you're second best!"
  "Ha ha, stop! No, don't stop. Louder!"
  "Thank you! That gave me goosebumps. On my goosebumps!"
@rule core.compliment.w_thank_slow guard: slow act: thank
  "Oh. {.}That's nice. I'll thank you properly in a minute."
  "Mmm. Thank you. I'm going to enjoy that one slowly."
  "Well, aren't you kind. {.}Thank you."
  "That was very sweet. Give me a second to glow."
@rule core.compliment.w_thank_quick guard: quick act: thank
  "Thanks! Gotta go! Kidding."
  "Ooh, nice, thank you, you're lovely, anyway, hi."
  "Aw thanks! I'd hug you but I'm mid-sentence."
@rule core.compliment.w_thank_elder guard: elder act: thank
  "Well, that's the nicest thing since the last nice thing."
  "Bless you. At my age, nobody says that. Say it again."
  "Thank you, dear. I'll tell my knees. They'll be thrilled."
  "Kind of you. I was starting to think I'd gone invisible."
@rule core.compliment.w_thank_teen guard: teen&!kid_speaker act: thank
  "Wait, really? Okay, thanks. That's actually nice."
  "I'm not blushing. It's warm in here. Thanks, though."
  "Huh. Cool, thanks. Don't make it weird."
  "Okay, that was good. I'm keeping it."
@rule core.compliment.w_thank_sad guard: mood=sad act: thank
  "Thank you. I really needed that today."
  "That's kind. I'm having a hard day, and that helped."
  "Oh. Thank you. That was the best thing I heard all week."
@rule core.compliment.w_thank_happy guard: mood=happy act: thank
  "Thank you! I'm having a great day and you just made it better."
  "Aw, I'm so happy right now. You made it better. Thanks."
  "My cheeks hurt from smiling. Blame yourself."
@rule core.compliment.w_thank_tired guard: mood=tired act: thank
  "Thank you. That just woke me up. Slightly."
  "Aww. Best thing I've heard since I last slept."
@rule core.compliment.w_thank_friend guard: rel=friend act: thank
  "Coming from you? That counts double."
  "You always know what to say. It's annoying. Thanks."
  "Okay, now I owe you a snack. A big snack."
  "You're good for me, you know that? Thanks."
@rule core.compliment.w_thank_night guard: night act: thank
  "That's a nice thing to hear in the dark. Thank you."
  "Thanks. A kind word at night is worth two in daylight."
@rule core.compliment.w_thank_hellborn guard: hellborn&!kid_speaker act: thank
  "Hm. In the pit, compliments are rarer than rain. Thank you."
  "My horns are tingling. That's how I know it's sincere."
  "Thanks. I'll remember that when the downstairs neighbours complain."
@rule core.compliment.w_thank_ghost guard: ghost act: thank
  "Aww. I'm glowing. More than usual, I mean."
  "That's so kind. I'd float, but I always do."
@rule core.compliment.w_thank_kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: thank
  "Really? Wow, thanks! I'm telling my whole class."
  "Yay! Thank you! That's my new favourite thing you said."
  "Hee hee! You're nice! Do you want a sticker?"
  "I did my best! I did my best and my best was good."
  "Thanks! Can you say it to my teacher too?"
  "Aw, thanks! I'll give you my second-best crayon."

# ---- COMPLIMENT: joke -------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.compliment.w_joke act: joke
  "I know, right? I'm basically a limited edition."
  "Careful, I bruise easily. Mostly my ego."
  "Please clap. {.}Fine, a small clap."
  "I was going to say the same about me, but you beat me to it."
  "Stop it, you'll make me insufferable. More insufferable."
  "I'm just a regular tamagotchi with extra steps."
  "Compliment accepted. Please deposit another to continue."
  "Is this a compliment or a very kind ambush?"
  "That's twice today! Once from me, and once from you."
  "Keep talking. I'm collecting these for my trophy shelf."
  "Say that again, but slower, and into this tiny recorder."
  "I wake up like this. It takes hours of practice."
@rule core.compliment.w_joke_blunt guard: blunt act: joke
  "Finally, someone with eyes."
  "Obviously. But go on."
  "Correct. Do you have more? I have time."
@rule core.compliment.w_joke_quirky guard: quirky act: joke
  "Is that so? The fish told me the same, and they're never wrong."
  "I'll add it to the wall of nice things. Next to the spoon."
  "A compliment! Quick, someone check it for pigeons."
@rule core.compliment.w_joke_easygoing guard: easygoing act: joke
  "Ha, cool. I'll take that with a side of nap."
  "Sure, why not. I'll be fabulous right after lunch."
@rule core.compliment.w_joke_serious guard: serious act: joke
  "Noted. I will accept it as a formal commendation."
  "I'll add that to my permanent record. Under accomplishments."
  "Please put that in writing. In triplicate. With stickers."

# ---- COMPLIMENT: return, tease, dismiss, laugh -------------------------------------------------
@rule core.compliment.w_return act: compliment
  "You first. You have a really nice, uh, whole thing going on."
  "Right back at you. Double. With a bow on it."
  "And you! Look at you, being all pleasant!"
  "Stop. You're making me say nice things back."
  "Oh, you're sweet. You're the sweetest thing in this zip code."
  "That's what I was about to say about you. Honest."
  "Nice! We're both great. What a coincidence."
  "I think you're swell. Isn't that a word? Swell?"
@rule core.compliment.w_return_polite guard: polite act: compliment
  "And you are an absolute delight, if I may say so."
  "Likewise, truly. You have a lovely way about you."
@rule core.compliment.w_return_friend guard: rel=friend act: compliment
  "Best friend energy. You've got loads of it."
  "Ugh, you're making me say it. You're awesome. There."
@rule core.compliment.w_tease act: tease
  "Flattery will get you everywhere. {.}What do you want?"
  "Is this a compliment, or are you about to ask for money?"
  "Aww. Did you rehearse that? You did, didn't you."
  "You're sucking up. It's working. Don't stop."
  "Easy there. My head doesn't fit in the doorway as it is."
  "Smooth talker. Do you do that for everyone, or just me?"
  "Okay, who sent you? I want to meet your boss."
  "That's the nicest thing you've said since never."
  "Look at you being charming. I'm filing a report."
@rule core.compliment.w_tease_rival guard: rel=rival act: tease
  "Are you being nice? Should I check for a trap?"
  "A compliment from you? I'm taking my wallet out of my pocket."
@rule core.compliment.w_dismiss act: dismiss
  "Eh, it's nothing. I just stood there."
  "Nah. I'm basically wallpaper. Nice wallpaper, though."
  "Oh, come on. It's just a Tuesday for me."
  "That's very kind. But I'm really not special."
  "Aw, you're just saying that. Thank you for saying that."
@rule core.compliment.w_dismiss_blunt guard: blunt act: dismiss
  "Don't flatter me. It's weird."
  "Sure. Whatever you need. Moving on."
@rule core.compliment.w_dismiss_flat guard: flat act: dismiss
  "Okay. Thanks. Let's not make it a thing."
  "Sure. I'll take it. Quietly."
@rule core.compliment.w_laugh act: laugh
  "Ha ha! Oh, that's too nice. I need a minute."
  "Ha! Okay, okay, you got me. I'm lovely."
  "Oh, stop, you're making me giggle. It's undignified."
  "Hee. Sorry, I laugh when I'm happy. It's a medical thing."

# ---- PRAISE_OTHER: agree ------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.praise_other.w_agree act: agree
  "Completely. They're a gem. A slightly chipped gem."
  "I was just thinking that! Great minds, tiny budget."
  "Absolutely. I'd say so to their face, but their face intimidates me."
  "Right? They're one of the good ones."
  "Totally. It's rare. Like finding a clean mug."
  "Yes! Somebody finally says it out loud."
  "I couldn't agree more. And I never agree."
  "Oh, for sure. We should give them a medal. A big one."
  "That's true. They deserve a little parade."
  "I've said that myself. In my head. Very loudly."
@rule core.praise_other.w_agree_polite guard: polite act: agree
  "How true. They are a credit to the neighbourhood."
  "Indeed. I always speak very warmly of them."
@rule core.praise_other.w_agree_friend guard: rel=friend act: agree
  "See, this is why we're friends. Good taste in people."
  "You and I think alike. Terrifying, honestly."
@rule core.praise_other.w_agree_loud guard: loud act: agree
  "YES! They're AMAZING. Somebody throw confetti!"
  "I love that you said that! I LOVE it!"
@rule core.praise_other.w_agree_elder guard: elder act: agree
  "I've known them for years. A fine soul. Mostly."
  "Hm, yes. Good people are scarcer than good soup."
@rule core.praise_other.w_agree_kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: agree
  "Yeah! They're so cool. I want to be them when I'm big!"
  "I think so too! They gave me a cookie once. A whole cookie!"

# ---- PRAISE_OTHER: disagree, joke, tease, gossip ----------------------------------------------
@rule core.praise_other.w_disagree act: disagree
  "Hm. Nice is a stretch. Tolerable, maybe."
  "I'd like to agree. I really do. I'll think about it."
  "Eh. Good days, bad days. Today's a medium day."
  "I wouldn't go that far. Maybe halfway. With a bus."
  "Well. They have their moments. Some of them are short."
@rule core.praise_other.w_disagree_blunt guard: blunt act: disagree
  "No. Overrated. Next."
  "Meh. I've seen better. I've seen toast with more charm."
@rule core.praise_other.w_disagree_polite guard: polite act: disagree
  "I'm afraid I see it a little differently. But I'm glad you do."
  "That's a lovely view. I'm not quite there myself."
@rule core.praise_other.w_joke act: joke
  "They're great. They don't know it. Let's not tell them."
  "Sure, they're great. At naps. They're an athlete."
  "Praise them any louder and they'll want a raise."
  "They're so great that the walls clap when they walk by."
  "They'd love to hear that. They won't, but they'd love to."
  "Great? They invented the word. Then lost it."
@rule core.praise_other.w_tease act: tease
  "Aww. You have a little crush on them, don't you."
  "Careful, I'm telling them you said that."
  "You're their biggest fan. Do you want a banner?"
  "Look at you being loyal. Tell me what they gave you."
@rule core.praise_other.w_gossip act: gossip
  "They are great. Between us, they once cried at a sandwich."
  "True, true. I heard they hum when nobody's around."
  "Yep. Though they were up very late last night. I won't say why."
  "Good one. I heard they make their own jam. In secret."

# ---- THANK: replies to the player's thanks --------------------------------------------------
@rule core.thank.w_answer act: answer
  "My pleasure. I'll bill you later. In hugs."
  "You're welcome. Don't mention it. Seriously, don't."
  "Anytime, friend. Or at least until my break."
  "Glad I could help. I'd do it again for a muffin."
  "No worries! That's what I'm here for. That and the snacks."
  "Of course. It was nothing. It was a little something, but still."
  "Happy to help. Really. It's good for my aura."
  "Oh, don't thank me. Thank my mother. She raised me right."
  "Any time. I mean it. I'm very bored."
  "You're very welcome. Say, are you hungry?"
  "Sure thing. Come back when you need something else."
  "That's what neighbours are for. That and complaining about the weather."
@rule core.thank.w_answer_polite guard: polite act: answer
  "It was no trouble at all. Truly."
  "You are most welcome. It was a pleasure."
  "Please, think nothing of it. I insist."
@rule core.thank.w_answer_flat guard: flat act: answer
  "You're welcome. {.}That was a smile. I swear."
  "Sure. No big deal. It's what I do."
  "Mm. Don't mention it. Yes, I mean that kindly."
@rule core.thank.w_answer_blunt guard: blunt act: answer
  "Yep. Fine. You're welcome."
  "Okay. Don't make it weird. You're welcome."
@rule core.thank.w_answer_loud guard: loud act: answer
  "Oh, ANYTIME! I mean it! Even at three AM!"
  "You are SO welcome! Seriously, ask again for fun."
@rule core.thank.w_answer_elder guard: elder act: answer
  "Of course, dear. You'd do the same for me. Or you'd better."
  "No trouble. I had nothing else planned. Thirty years, nothing."
@rule core.thank.w_answer_friend guard: rel=friend act: answer
  "Always. That's the deal with us, isn't it?"
  "You don't have to thank me. But I'll take it anyway."
@rule core.thank.w_answer_kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: answer
  "You're welcome! I'm a good helper! Right?"
  "Yay, I helped! Do I get a sticker? A small one?"
  "No problem! I do this all the time, mostly by accident."
@rule core.thank.w_joke act: joke
  "You're welcome. The tip jar is on the left."
  "I'd say it was nothing, but I did a lot of nothing for you."
  "Thanks accepted. Please take a number for the next one."
  "Aw. Thank me again, I need it for my morale quota."
  "Thanks noted and filed under 'I'm the best.'"
  "Say that again. I'm collecting them. I have two."
@rule core.thank.w_tease act: tease
  "Wow, thank me a few more times, it's a real bonding moment."
  "Is this the part where you owe me a favour? I'll think of one."
  "You said please and thanks in one day. Who are you?"
  "I'm going to need that in writing, with a seal."
@rule core.thank.w_backchannel act: backchannel
  "Mm-hm. Anytime."
  "Sure. Yep."
  "Aw. Of course."
  "Mhm. Glad it worked out."
@rule core.thank.w_dismiss act: dismiss
  "Pfft. It's nothing. Forget it."
  "Don't mention it. Really. I'll forget by lunch."
  "Oh, hush. It's fine. We're good."
